Dev-Log #1

- Changed the radar to B-SCOPE style

    Added Bearing, Range, Altitude measuring to radar (BRA)

This is a standard military combat shorthand format 
used to pinpoint a target's location relative to your aircraft. 
It stands for Bearing (direction in degrees), 
Range (distance in nautical miles), and Altitude (height of the contact)


    Added "Radar Mode" measuring to radar (MODE)

This displays the current tracking or scanning sub-mode 
the radar is operating under, often combined with information 
like expected target speed thresholds (such as knots).


    Added "Channel" measuring to radar(CHAN)

This displays the active data link channel frequency 
being used to share tactical info with friendly aircraft.
